O_{i})$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$32$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $1 \\mathrm{\\% }$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The sample data fit a binomial distribution $B(4, p)$\n- $H_{1}$: The sample data does not fit a binomial distribution $B(4, p)$\n\nUse this data to calculate an estimate of $p$."] [:db/cas 17592186162506 :question/problem "A university chemistry professor measures students' grades from $0$ to $100$ points. A random sample of students is taken, and the frequency distribution of the students' grades is shown below.\n\n| Students' grades | $0 \\le y_{i} < 30$ | $30 \\le y_{i} < 50$ | $50 \\le y_{i} < 80$ | $80 \\le y_{i} \\le 100$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Observed Frequency $(O_{i})$ | $10$ | $13$ | $17$ | $10$ |\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $5 \\mathrm{\\% }$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The students' grades are distributed uniformly.\n- $H_{1}$: The students' grades are not distributed uniformly.\n\nCalculate the value of the test statistic for this hypothesis test. Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\nRounded to three decimal places, the value of the test statistic is {{field-1}}.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." "A university chemistry professor measures students' grades from $0$ to $100$ points. A random sample of students is taken, and the frequency distribution of the students' grades is shown below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"left\" data-fill=