od. The table below shows the number of calls received per minute and their corresponding frequencies.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Calls</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\ge 4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $5 \\mathrm{\\% }$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The sample data fit a Poisson distribution $Po(λ)$\n- $H_{1}$: The sample data do not fit a Poisson distribution $Po(λ)$\n\nUse this data to calculate an estimate for the rate $λ$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [:db/cas 17592186162511 :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a random variable with support $S = {0, 1, 2, 3, …}$. A random sample is carried out, and the sample data is shown below.\n\n| Observation $(y_{i})$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $\\ge 4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Observed Frequency $(O_{i})$ | $16$ | $27$ | $17$ | $8$ | $0$ |\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $1 \\mathrm{\\% }$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}:Y∼Po(λ)$\n- $H_{1}:Y≁Po(λ)$\n\nUse this data to calculate an estimator for the rate $λ$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." "Suppose $Y$ is a random variable